WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.800
Imagine your household's
income rises by 10 per cent.

2
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:05.420
Maybe you eat out more.

3
00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:07.550
Maybe you book a holiday abroad.

4
00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:11.480
But a few things in your weekly
spending would quietly shrink.

5
00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.250
So when people get richer,

6
00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:16.940
why do they buy more of some
things but less of others?

7
00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:21.150
In this mission, you'll measure how
strongly demand responds to income,

8
00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:22.750
using one number.

9
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:26.150
Then you'll raise incomes
in three markets at once

10
00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:28.670
and watch every demand curve move.

11
00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:32.290
Your mission: find out which
goods people leave behind

12
00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:33.490
as they get richer.
